Slide 6: Live Case Study 3 – Innovation & Scale (Amazon & Tata Steel)
•	Estimated Time: 1 minute 45 seconds
•	What to Say:
"At Amazon, leaders use a process called Working Backwards. Before a single line of code is written or a dollar is spent building a new product, the team must write an imaginary press release and customer FAQ. If the press release doesn't sound compelling to a real customer, the project is killed or redesigned right there. They engineer quality in before building anything.Similarly, look at Tata Steel. Facing intense global competition, leadership embedded Total Quality Management across every level—creating thousands of shop-floor 'quality circles' where frontline workers solved operational bottlenecks. That cultural shift made Tata Steel the first integrated steelmaker outside Japan to win the prestigious Deming Prize, transforming it into one of the highest-quality, lowest-cost producers in the world."
•	Transition: "So, how do we take lessons from Toyota, Ritz-Carlton, Amazon, and Tata Steel and apply them to our own teams?"
