Slide 7: The Leader’s Daily Playbook
•	Estimated Time: 1 minute 30 seconds
•	What to Say:
"You don't need a massive budget to lead like this. Here are three habits you can start practicing this week:
1.	Go to the Gemba: Gemba is a Japanese term meaning 'the real place.' Don't manage purely from spreadsheets in a conference room. Walk the floor, listen to customer calls, and observe where the actual work happens.
2.	Ask 'Why?' Five Times: When something breaks, don't stop at the first easy excuse. Ask 'Why did that happen?' five times in a row until you uncover the broken process underneath.
3.	Reward Transparency: The next time someone on your team brings you bad news early, don't shoot the messenger. Thank them for giving you the chance to fix it while it's still small."
•	Transition: "That brings us to our final thought today."
